Z||000007||FieroJoe||02-24-2001||06:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>To keep your hands warm when you push it.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ok, ya stumped me on that one...<P>I put in a power trunk release into my 87 coupe, and got the bezel with the defogger switch in it.  My uncle helped me then build a circuit with 3 relays that make the normally momentary defogger switch act as a normal on/off switch.  You push the button to "ON", the little indicator light comes on, and my fog lights come on.  Push it to "off", lights go out.  Even the panel light will come on when the lights are on.  Now all I need to find is a little icon of fog lights and see if I can put on in there...any ideas?<BR><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroJoe||02-24-2001||06:51 PM||||hmm, just popped off the cover to the switch and looked at the icon, It's been melted into there at the factory.  Id have to have another one before I started messing with it, just in case.||||reg||1
